  "body": "MAINLINE-022d complete; QUESTIONABLE throughout. All 32 combinations have overall and half-wave-constrained optima: 64 full SF, binding-mode, spacing and mass rows. Both Zylon plies are charged. Ti/CFRP joint dimensions and mass use each candidate's multiplier. Film gauge is continuous; tensile bending is constrained at Ft=15.586 MPa, PROJECTION.\n\nBest equilateral overall: Zylon/CFRP, cap, 5% reserve, SF 1.397732582 at s=6.085747 m, half-wave/member=0.569022. Best equilateral screened: SF 1.258252477 at s=3.170759 m; local/global/film bind. Its masses are tubes 4183.590, film 214.542, joints 44.191, nodes 2.927, systems 100, reserve 244.472 and sag lift loss 99.720 kg. Membrane screened SF is 1.251857092; 019 reserve gives 1.194121426 cap and 1.187857743 membrane.\n\nThe two-way surrogate numerically leads at 2.010980577 overall and 1.867825477 screened, but its missing shear stiffness leaves those capacities unqualified. Square-cell sag/wave sensitivity lowers the latter to 1.728882831. Passing one-member half-wave is only the requested screen.\n\nSixteen overall optima fail that screen. Independent reconstruction passes 2800 checks; 112 optimized sensitivity witnesses and eleven open NFI are filed. Wider bounds improve none of sixteen checked cap optima. Qualified full-size allowable and assembly failure probability remain unknown. No next job.",
